netfilter: nft_set_pipapo: prefer kvmalloc for scratch maps

jira KERNEL-1646
Rebuild_History Non-Buildable kernel-5.14.0-687.51.1.el9_8
commit-author Florian Westphal <fw@strlen.de>
commit 897eefee2eb73ec6c119a0ca357d7b4a3e92c5ef
Empty-Commit: Cherry-Pick Conflicts during history rebuild.
Will be included in final tarball splat. Ref for failed cherry-pick at:
ciq/ciq_backports/kernel-5.14.0-687.51.1.el9_8/897eefee.failed

The scratchmap size depends on the number of elements in the set.
For huge sets, each scratch map can easily require very large
allocations, e.g. for 100k entries each scratch map will require
close to 64kbyte of memory.

	Signed-off-by: Florian Westphal <fw@strlen.de>
	Reviewed-by: Stefano Brivio <sbrivio@redhat.com>
	Signed-off-by: Pablo Neira Ayuso <pablo@netfilter.org>
(cherry picked from commit 897eefee2eb73ec6c119a0ca357d7b4a3e92c5ef)
	Signed-off-by: Jonathan Maple <jmaple@ciq.com>

